Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 11/13/2024]
1. Resonance energies are calculated from Ex values listed in ENSDF 2022.
2. Experimental spectroscopic factors are adopted from the 31Si mirror states (Endt 1990).
3. Gamma-ray partial widths are estimated using the measured lifetimes of the 31Si mirror states; see Wrede et al. (2009).
3. Er = 2155 keV: the corresponding 31Cl level at Ex = 2418 keV is assigned to the Ex = 2317 keV 31Si mirror (3/2+). This assignment is the most likely possibility,
   but it is not unambiguous.
4. Direct capture to the ground state is estimated using the average experimental spectroscopic factor of the 31Si mirror level (Endt 1990).
